CYFR Licensing
==============

This project uses mixed per-file licensing. The default license is
**Apache License 2.0**; files under `apps/cyfr/lib/sanctum/` (Sanctum — the auth, policy,
and tenancy layer) and the matching tests under `apps/cyfr/test/sanctum/`
are licensed under the **Functional Source License, Version 1.1,
Apache 2.0 Future License** (FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0). Everything else,
including the tenancy schema migrations, is Apache-2.0.

The boundary is the directory: everything under `apps/cyfr/lib/sanctum/`
and `apps/cyfr/test/sanctum/` is FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0, and everything else
in the repo is Apache-2.0. Elixir files carry an in-band
`SPDX-License-Identifier` header (there is no `REUSE.toml`). The canonical
license texts live in the `LICENSES/` directory, and the FSL zone is
enforced mechanically by `.github/workflows/license-lint.yml`.

* `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt` — Apache License 2.0 (OSI-approved).
* `LICENSES/FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0.txt` — the canonical, unmodified
  Functional Source License 1.1 with Apache 2.0 as the future license.

The FSL restricts third parties from offering CYFR — or substantially the
same functionality — as a competing commercial product or service.
Internal use is unrestricted. The FSL also irrevocably grants an
additional Apache 2.0 license to each released version of an FSL file,
effective two years after that version is made available; any revision at
least two years old may be used under Apache 2.0.

See `FAIR_SOURCE.md` and the `README.md` "License" section for the
practical implications for self-hosting, distributing, and contributing.

Copyright 2026 CYFR Works Inc.
